@flexiarg apparatus/fix-order-with-behaviour-spec
@title Order the Fix and State the Behaviour That Defines Fixed
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-8LFNR7 turn-ZKKD1Q; first proposed for: Immediately after a failure report and a delegated diagnosis (turn-zZk0DV), the operator orders the repair.
@why [stack-coherence/commit-intent-alignment]

! conclusion: Issue the fix directive and pair it with the observable behaviour that counts as fixed, not with implementation steps.

  + IF:
    A tool has misbehaved and its correct behaviour is known to the operator.

  + HOWEVER:
    A bare 'fix it' leaves done-ness undefined; an over-specified fix micromanages the repair.

  + THEN:
    Issue the fix directive and pair it with the observable behaviour that counts as fixed, not with implementation steps.

  + BECAUSE:
    commit-intent-alignment asks that stated intent and enacted change line up; this narrows it to repair directives: the acceptance criterion is stated as behaviour ('voxterm should know that') so the fix can be checked against intent.
